<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lygdamis I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Lygdamis I of Halicarnassus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lygdamis I was a ruler of Halicarnassus in Caria at the end of the 6th century BCE, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>, and the founder of a dynasty of Carian descent. He was the father of Queen Artemisia I, who fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xerxes-i">Xerxes</a> at Salamis in 480 BCE, and grandfather of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lygdamis-ii">Lygdamis II</a>, the tyrant who drove the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lygdamis-i.jpg" alt="Lygdamis I" width="320" height="132" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CARIA,_Mylasa._Circa_520-490_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
